K325T: port of MiSTer-devel/Minimig-AGA_MiSTer 8813609 (class b: changes OCS/ECS behaviour), ADAPTED
"Fix blitter (Deep Core CD32 background)" (#287), Agnus / blitter / bridge part (the ddram_ctrl part is
MiSTer-only), at AExp line positions: while a blit runs with BLTPRI set, a CPU write to a blitter
register is not acknowledged until the blit is over.  Upstream evidence: Deep Core (CD32, 68EC020
running from its cache wrote into a running blit).  Adapted: only with the 68020 (cpucfg[1]).  For
the 68000 upstream's rule is stricter than the chip: a BLTPRI blit leaves its unused bus cycles
(e.g. every second cycle of a D-only blit) to the CPU, so a write lands mid-blit (tools/mk_a500probe.py
test 7: 16 CCK around the write without the hold, 8206 CCK with it).  The A500 machine (fx68k) keeps
that behaviour.
